### High-order derivative training on a seed closure, not the dense set:
### the carried multi-indices are the downward closure of alpha_seeds.dat.
### target u(x) = prod_i sin(omega_i x_i + phi_i), see tools/gen_hod_train.f90
Rand_seed    20260803 / fixed seed (reproducibility)
Restart     0 /
Output_deriv 1 / write output_hod.datXXXX at the end
Init_w      LeCun_unif
Nlayer      4 / L
4 / ndim(1) = D0
6 /
6 /
1 / ndim(L) (must be 1 for MATH_HOD)
###
Loss_term  HOD_DATA      80  train.dat          1.d0 /
###
Hod_K 7 / max order K; lambda_p = 1/(p!)^2 (Taylor-coefficient normalization)
1.000000e+00  / lambda_0 = 1/(p!)^2
1.000000e+00  / lambda_1 = 1/(p!)^2
2.500000e-01  / lambda_2 = 1/(p!)^2
2.777778e-02  / lambda_3 = 1/(p!)^2
1.736111e-03  / lambda_4 = 1/(p!)^2
6.944444e-05  / lambda_5 = 1/(p!)^2
1.929012e-06  / lambda_6 = 1/(p!)^2
3.936760e-08  / lambda_7 = 1/(p!)^2
Hod_check 1 / run self-tests [G][F][W] before fitting
Hod_alpha_file alpha_seeds.dat /
###
Num_validation 10 /
Validation_cyc 50 /
P_max 10000 /
###
Epoch      10000 /
Activation TANH / required for MATH_HOD
Conv       1.d-8 /
Num_batch  10 /
Checkpoint_cyc         1000 /
GD_method  Adam
GD_param   0.002d0 0.9d0 0.999d0 1.d-8 0.d0 /
